.TH OFFLINE-GPG 7 "" "offline NixOS image" "Miscellaneous Information Manual"
.SH NAME
offline-gpg \- managing GnuPG keys on the air-gapped offline image
.SH DESCRIPTION
This image is booted from a USB drive on a machine that stays disconnected from every network.
Its purpose is to hold the secret key of an OpenPGP identity, so that the key never touches the networked machine.
The image provides GnuPG, paperkey, KeePassXC, the YubiKey tools and a printer driver for paper backups.
.PP
Networking is disabled.
Wi-Fi and Bluetooth kernel modules are blacklisted, and NetworkManager is not running.
Files enter and leave the machine only on removable media.
.SH IMPORTING THE SECRET KEY
Plug in the drive that holds the exported secret key and find its device with
.BR lsblk (8).
Mount it with
.BR "udisksctl mount \-b /dev/sdX1" .
Mounted drives appear under
.IR /run/media/nixos/ .
Import the key with
.PP
.RS
.nf
gpg \-\-import /run/media/nixos/DRIVE/secret-key.asc
.fi
.RE
.PP
or with
.PP
.RS
.nf
offline\-gpg import /run/media/nixos/DRIVE/secret-key.asc
.fi
.RE
.PP
GnuPG asks for the passphrase of the key through its pinentry dialogue.
The imported keys are kept in a temporary home directory that is lost on shutdown.
.SH CHECKING EXPIRY DATES
List the secret keys with
.PP
.RS
.nf
gpg \-\-list\-secret\-keys \-\-keyid\-format long
.fi
.RE
.PP
Each primary key and subkey line ends in the expiry date, in the form
.BR "[SC] [expires: 2027-01-31]" .
The recipe
.B list-keys
runs the same command.
.SH EXTENDING THE EXPIRY
The command
.PP
.RS
.nf
gpg\-extend\-expiry [\-o FILE] FINGERPRINT [EXPIRY]
.fi
.RE
.PP
sets the expiry of the primary key and of all subkeys of the secret key FINGERPRINT.
EXPIRY is any form that gpg accepts, such as
.BR 1y ,
.B 90d
or
.BR 2030\-01\-01 .
It defaults to one year, counted from the current date.
The command then prints the new expiry dates and writes the armoured public key to
.IR FINGERPRINT .pub.asc
in the current directory, or to FILE when
.B \-o
is given.
The command fails if FINGERPRINT is not a secret key in the keyring.
.PP
The environment variable
.B GPG_OPTS
holds extra options for every gpg invocation.
It is split on whitespace, and a lone
.B ''
stands for an empty argument.
.PP
The command is equivalent to the following raw gpg invocations.
The first changes the primary key and the second changes all subkeys.
.PP
.RS
.nf
gpg \-\-quick\-set\-expire FINGERPRINT 1y
gpg \-\-quick\-set\-expire FINGERPRINT 1y '*'
.fi
.RE
.PP
The system clock of an offline machine is often wrong.
Check the date with
.BR date (1)
before extending the expiry, because the new expiry is computed from it.
.SH MOVING THE PUBLIC KEY BACK
Copy the file
.IR FINGERPRINT .pub.asc
to removable media, shut the image down, and import it on the networked machine with
.PP
.RS
.nf
gpg \-\-import FINGERPRINT.pub.asc
.fi
.RE
.PP
The updated key can then be published, for example with
.BR "gpg \-\-send\-keys FINGERPRINT" ,
or uploaded to any other service that holds the key.
.PP
If the subkeys live on a YubiKey or another OpenPGP card, the card holds only the secret subkeys.
Extending the expiry changes the self-signatures on the public key and nothing on the card.
No transfer to the card is needed.
The networked machine needs the updated public key so that it accepts signatures made with the subkeys.
.SH PAPERKEY BACKUP AND PRINTING
The program
.BR paperkey (1)
extracts the secret parts of a key into a short text that can be stored on paper.
Create the text file with
.PP
.RS
.nf
gpg \-\-export\-secret\-keys FINGERPRINT | paperkey \-\-output FINGERPRINT.paperkey.txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Print it with
.PP
.RS
.nf
lp FINGERPRINT.paperkey.txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Restoring from paper requires the public key as well as the paperkey text.
.SH OFFLINE-GPG RECIPES
The command
.B offline\-gpg
runs recipes from the justfile
.IR /etc/offline\-gpg/justfile .
Files are read from and written to the current directory.
.B offline\-gpg \-\-list
lists the recipes.
.TP
.B list\-keys
List the secret keys with fingerprints and expiry dates.
.TP
.BI import " PATH"
Import a secret key from PATH.
.TP
.BI generate " [NAME_AND_EMAIL]"
Generate a new master key and subkeys with
.BR gpg\-quick\-generate\-master\-key .
.TP
.BI extend\-expiry " FPR [EXPIRY]"
Run
.BR gpg\-extend\-expiry .
EXPIRY defaults to 1y.
.TP
.BI export\-public " FPR"
Write the armoured public key to
.IR FPR .pub.asc.
.TP
.BI backup\-paperkey " FPR [PRINT]"
Write a paperkey text backup to
.IR FPR .paperkey.txt.
Any value for PRINT also prints the file with
.BR lp (1).
.TP
.B card\-status
Show the status of the connected OpenPGP card.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gpg (1),
.BR paperkey (1)
